<article class="env-lemma" id="0DLA">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DLA">Lemma <span data-tag="0DLA">85.35.2</span>.</a> Let $X$ be an algebraic space over a scheme $S$. Let $a : U \to X$ be an fppf hypercovering. Suppose given $K_0 \in D_\mathit{QCoh}(U_0)$ and an isomorphism </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \alpha : L(f_{\delta _1^1})^*K_0 \longrightarrow L(f_{\delta _0^1})^*K_0  \]
</div>
  <p> satisfying the cocycle condition on $U_1$. Set $\tau ^ n_ i : [0] \to [n]$, $0 \mapsto i$ and set $K_ n = Lf_{\tau ^ n_ n}^*K_0$. Assume $\mathop{\mathrm{Ext}}\nolimits ^ i_{\mathcal{O}_{U_ n}}(K_ n, K_ n) = 0$ for $i < 0$. Then there exists an object $K \in D_\mathit{QCoh}(\mathcal{O}_ X)$ and an isomorphism $La_0^*K \to K$ compatible with $\alpha $. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The objects $K_ n$ form the members of a simplicial system of the derived category of modules by Lemma <a href="/tag/0GMF" data-tag="0GMF">85.14.3</a>. Then we obtain an object $K' \in D_\mathit{QCoh}(\mathcal{O}_{U_{\acute{e}tale}})$ such that $(K_ n, K_\varphi )$ is the system deduced from $K'$, see Lemma <a href="/tag/0D9T" data-tag="0D9T">85.14.7</a>. Finally, we apply Lemma <a href="/tag/0DHF" data-tag="0DHF">85.34.4</a> to see that $K' = La^*K$ for some $K \in D_\mathit{QCoh}(\mathcal{O}_ X)$ as desired. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>